WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.860
Did "Shazam: Fury of the Gods" catch lightning
in a bottle again or is it just another overblown,

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.830
overstuffed sequel?

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.740
Twitter's surprising reactions are pouring
in.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:15.330
As James Gunn and Peter Safran prepare to
kick off the revamped DC Universe — leaving

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:20.330
the DC Extended Universe largely behind — we're
witnessing the final few releases that were

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.300
greenlit prior to their hiring.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.029
Before we get to check out fellow holdouts
like "The Flash" and "Aquaman and the Lost

00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:30.269
Kingdom," we'll get to meet up with the Shazamily
once again for "Shazam!

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:31.660
Fury of the Gods."

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:36.620
This sequel to the 2019 film sees Shazam and
his superpowered family take on godly new

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.100
foes who threaten the entire world.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.760
Ahead of the release of "Fury of the Gods,"
some critics were fortunate enough to see

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.480
the sequel early, going on to post their reviews
online so potential moviegoers know what to

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.570
expect from it.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.899
Overall, most are in agreement that it's,
well, just fine.

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:56.050
It has its big moments and gives you what
you would want from a Shazam adventure, but

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.780
ultimately fails to surpass its predecessor.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:01.899
Of course, these assessments come from a small
group of critics.

00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:06.430
What does the wider DC and Shazam fanbase
think about this long-awaited continuation?

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:09.160
Thankfully, for those curious, reactions to
"Shazam!

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:13.130
Fury of the Gods" from the general public
have begun to pop up on Twitter..

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:17.731
Based on the earliest reactions, it has become
even more clear than it already was that fans

00:01:17.731 --> 00:01:20.189
and critics don't always see eye-to-eye.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:24.967
Many folks on the social media platform have
been quick to voice their support for the sequel.

00:01:24.967 --> 00:01:26.470
One user wrote:

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:28.150
"Shazam Fury of the Gods is a lot of fun.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:32.759
Idk if it was better than the first movie,
but the villains and the action were definitely

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:33.829
a step up."

00:01:33.829 --> 00:01:38.430
They also enjoyed the film's handful of surprises
and two post-credits scenes.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:42.640
Another user rated the sequel a 10 out of
10 and highlighted the comedy as one of its

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.100
strongest elements.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.100
That seemed to be a common theme, with other
Twitter users chiming in with their appreciation

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.479
for the movie's comedic side.

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:53.990
A lot of people seem to be fans of the new
characters and worldbuilding elements as well.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:56.539
"Okay, I feel like maybe I should be writing
all this down."

00:01:56.539 --> 00:02:01.100
Fans are certainly admitting that "Fury of
the Gods" has its flaws, but they don't outweigh

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.100
the positives.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.280
As one user said:

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.380
"It's these amazing characters sprinkled with
a heavy dose of heart that makes it all worthwhile.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:13.160
SHAZAM FURY OF THE GODS is endearing, hilarious,
entertaining and epic.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:17.010
Helen Mirren stands out as a great addition
to Shazam's roster."

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.590
They also note that it's a crowd-pleaser that
goes bigger than the first "Shazam!"

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.360
movie and packs in some big twists.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:27.349
At the same time, just because some DC fans
aren't in sync with the critical consensus

00:02:27.349 --> 00:02:28.980
doesn't mean all of them are.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:32.361
People have also taken to Twitter to express
their disappointment in "Shazam!

00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:35.060
Fury of the Gods" for one reason or another.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:38.790
One user voiced their exhaustion with comic
book movies of this style, posting,

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.739
"What made Shazam unique was portraying a
kid endowed with powers.

00:02:42.739 --> 00:02:48.042
That is almost completely abandoned here for
yet another 2hrs of good capes punching bad capes."

00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:54.113
Other users weren't impressed either, specifically
calling out the film's VFX shots as unforgettably rough.

00:02:54.113 --> 00:02:58.640
Meanwhile, one fan had multiple complaints
about the sequel, ranging from the pacing

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.990
to what they considered to be a total misuse
of Helen Mirren and Lucy Liu.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.551
"We end this now."

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.289
"Yeah, we do."

00:03:07.289 --> 00:03:12.302
At the end of the day, reading Twitter reactions
to a movie is no way to form an opinion on it.

00:03:12.302 --> 00:03:14.731
If you wanna really figure out where you stand
on "Shazam!

00:03:14.731 --> 00:03:18.230
Fury of the Gods," the best way to do so is
to check it out yourself.

